using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}},\\,{{field-4}}\\le y\\le {{field-5}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points $P(x,y)$ satisfy the condition\n\n$$\nx\\in {-3,-2,-1},\\,y\\in {-4,-3,-2,-1}.\n$$\n\nIn other words,\n\n$$\n-3\\le x\\le -1,\\,-4\\le y\\le -1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le -1,\\,-4\\le y\\le -1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, Two Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25ad51f9-40e4-58cb-8b09-916587ea0e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285119} {:answer/id #uuid "2f3d8b94-54ad-59ce-880f-d51063153c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285214} {:answer/id #uuid "4e8334ca-8dca-57de-8515-429ca333129d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285516} {:answer/id #uuid "a281bf13-7094-575b-998a-0ab16373d6fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286278} {:answer/id #uuid "acc26dd4-18f5-5dc5-aec6-8f3f5c54644d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e8334ca-8dca-57de-8515-429ca333129d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 175921862